id: pmc-hound-generated-dist
title: Stop Hound from linting generated dist/ output
description: "Disable Hound JSHint using the pm-slack and pm-web precedent: committed dist/ JavaScript targets ES2022, while Hound defaults to ES5 and produces false positives."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: ci,review-bots
created_at: "2026-10-27T02:00:21.789Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T08:55:50.124Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T08:55:48.718Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-27T07:21:18.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Hound no longer lints generated dist/ output; no other lint or gate changes
resolution: "Merged PR #290 at 3a9f5fbc2375c6f911d41cefd6df7f599be13cc1; inspected .hound.yml and ran node -e \"require('node:assert/strict').match(require('node:fs').readFileSync('.hound.yml','utf8'), /^jshint:\\n  enabled: false\\s*$/m)\" on main. Hound JSHint is explicitly disabled for generated ES2022 output. The merged configuration leaves package lint and release gates unchanged."
expected_result: Hound no longer lints generated dist/ output; no other lint or gate changes
actual_result: Hound JSHint is explicitly disabled for generated ES2022 output. The merged configuration leaves package lint and release gates unchanged.
